\subsection{Short English statement}
Find a constitutive model that explains sustained oscillation of a sphere settling through a wormlike micellar fluid.

\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Exactly analyzes a passive Maxwell-type settling closure and proves that every oscillation decays, including the zero-inertia limit.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Testing a passive one-relaxation closure.} Let $v$ be settling velocity and $s$ an additional drag stress. The simplest Maxwell-type reduced model is
\[
 m\dot v=F-\zeta v-s,\qquad \tau\dot s+s=\eta v,
\]
with constant driving $F$, $\zeta,\tau>0$, $\eta\geq0$, and $m\geq0$. Its equilibrium is $v_*=F/(\zeta+\eta)$, $s_*=\eta v_*$. For $m>0$ the characteristic polynomial of perturbations is
\[
 m\tau\lambda^2+(m+\zeta\tau)\lambda+(\zeta+\eta).
\]
Both roots have negative real part: if real, their product is positive and sum negative; if conjugate, each real part is half the negative sum. Oscillations, when the discriminant is negative, therefore decay.

\paragraph{The low-inertia limit is even more restrictive.} At $m=0$, substitute $v=(F-s)/\zeta$ into the stress equation. It becomes a scalar linear relaxation with rate $(1+\eta/\zeta)/\tau>0$. There is no nonconstant periodic solution. These assertions can also be checked directly from the matrix exponential or the single exponential at $m=0$.

\paragraph{Attempt outcome.} This rules out sustained oscillation in this particular passive linear closure; it does not rule out viscoelasticity or wormlike-micelle models generally. The observed nontransient phenomenon needs an ingredient absent here, such as nonlinear structural feedback, more state variables or spatial instability. Selecting such an ingredient from micellar breakage/recombination physics, deriving the sphere-fluid coupling and validating a stable oscillation remain unproved. Merely obtaining complex eigenvalues in a linearization would only explain transient ringing and is insufficient for the original target.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked positive coefficients, real and complex roots, m=0 and eta=0 boundaries; separated transient ringing from a stable periodic state. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked positive coefficients, real and complex roots, m=0 and eta=0 boundaries; separated transient ringing from a stable periodic state. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; A physically derived nonlinear or spatial micellar mechanism supporting sustained oscillation has not been constructed.

Coordinator checked the characteristic polynomial, signs of the roots and scalar zero-inertia reduction of the passive relaxation model. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 was used for file preparation and structural checks; no numerical experiment or theorem prover was used. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. A physically derived nonlinear or spatial micellar mechanism supporting sustained oscillation has not been constructed.

